scaped — then another, then a flood of starlight, pouring back to the Whispering Glade. the Grumble King shrank with every star, smaller, smaller, till only a grumble remained. The Grumble King, indeed."}, {'n': 4, 'title': 'Starlight Restored', 'text': "kindness is magic — Ivy wrote it in the family book, under the date, in the careful letters of someone who means it forever.\n\nthe Grumble King's grumble was kept in a jar on the mantel, as a reminder. On quiet nights it mutters. Ivy finds it comforting: proof that dark can be made small, and kept.\n\na feather of fire chose to stay with Ivy — or Ivy chose to stay with it; by now they weren't sure there was a difference. It sits by the bed, glowing softly, a nightlight of pure story."}, {'n': 5, 'title': 'The Promise Kept', 'text': "the Whispering Glade thrives: the enchanted forest enchants, the glade whispers kindly, the meadow moonlights. All because one child picked up a feather of fire and one friend said 'together.'\n\na wise owl is older now, greyer, no less brave. They still walk together, still argue about the ballad, still keep the grumble-jar dusted. Friendship, like starlight, doesn't fade if you tend it.\n\nkindness is magic. In the Whispering Glade, in the starlight, in every heart that hears the tale: the promise kept, the story told, the magic real."}, {'n': 6, 'title': 'Bedtime', 'text': 'Sleep tight, the Whispering Glade. The dark is just the blanket. The light is a feather of fire, and a feather of fire is here, and Ivy is here, and a wise owl is here.\n\nkindness is magic. Goodnight.\n\nIvy smiles from the doorway. Outside, the stars are out — all of them, every one, back where they belong. The brook sings. The fireflies dance.'}]}

